::MCQ::
What does the metacharacter * (Asterisk) represent in regex?
{
~ Matches exactly one character
= Matches zero or more occurrences of the preceding character or group
~ Matches one or more occurrences of the preceding character or group
~ Matches the start of a string
}

::MCQ::
Which Python module is primarily used for working with regular expressions?
{
~ regex
= re
~ pattern
~ string
}

::MCQ::
What is the purpose of the re.sub() function?
{
~ To search for patterns
~ To split text
~ To validate input
= To replace substrings matching a pattern
}

::MCQ::
The re.split() function can only split text based on whitespace.
{
~ True
= False 
}

::MCQ::
Regular expressions can be used for input validation.
{
= True
~ False 
}

::MCQ::
The + metacharacter matches zero occurrences of a preceding character.
{
~ True
= False 
}
